  "limitations": [
    "Measurements are one cold/reuse pair per host on the same physical machine, with Windows/Debian and some verification processes overlapping. They are named-workload measurements, not isolated statistical benchmarks or complete cold compiler-preparation timings. Peak working set was not measured.",
    "The retained stager WVB was compiled from current source in the earlier compact-frame batch and independently reproduced on each host here. Its Profile-8 applications were built with the source-built compact stager, then rebuilt via the normal refreshed wrappers. The earlier Profile-7 stager used to start this cycle remains an ignored diagnostic artifact, not another normal tool path.",
    "The staging-only selection proves retained-WVB-to-native reconstruction and behavior; it does not silently compile source or reconstruct unchanged linker/transport applications. The real Project 4 source-compilation runs provide the separate source-to-WVB evidence. The usage-only empty-path rejection was tightened after the valid reconstruction run and checked separately.",
    "Final analysis cache tests add rejection of mismatched republished source before cache publication. The earlier real timing pair preceded that additional guard and is not used for the final performance claim. Initial unit verification rejected an unexpected seventh cache file correctly; the test was corrected to accept the bounded-inventory diagnostic.",
    "Analyzer, Node, mode, implementation and all six authenticated input identities bind analysis reuse. Fresh admission and authentication occur before lookup; Foreign binding/pairing and emission remain later phases. Cached products are bounded, hash-validated and copied into private files. Existing complete WVB caches still bind their full producing graph.",
    "Focused verification comprises staging reconstruction, compiler-scale staging, the existing cache suite, final analysis-cache cases, production ingress sentinels, real paired-host compilation, routing and documentation validation. The automatic broad routing plan was not run locally: it expands to historical full-product reconstruction and library/database owners. Complete dual-host qualification is separate pending evidence and the prior exact-artifact qualification is not claimed for the refreshed bytes.",
    "No entire cold compiler preparation or packaging-tool source refresh was repeated. Existing successful caches were retained. Updating producer pins deliberately invalidates dependent product keys; current-source compiler and publisher preparation can still be expensive on their first miss. Native packaging and broader frozen-product reconstruction remain performance and qualification work.",
    "Generated diagnostics and intermediate outputs remain locally under ignored Artifacts/Work; retained staging WVB and host executables are repository artifacts. Exact commands, producer identities, result records and workload sizes are recorded for reproduction."
  ],
